  "worked_solution": "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{3}{5}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{(1\\times 5)+3}{5}=\\frac{8}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, we can multiply the two numbers. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{5}\\times \\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{8\\times 2}{5\\times 3}=\\frac{16}{15}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{16}{15}=1\\,\\text{R}1=1\\,\\frac{1}{15}\n$$",
